WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.694
AI agents can face many threat types.

2
00:00:02.694 --> 00:00:08.701
Prompt injection may manipulate the model into ignoring intended instructions or misusing tools.

3
00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:18.798
Indirect prompt injection may hide malicious instructions inside documents, web pages, emails, tickets, repository content, or retrieved knowledge.

4
00:00:18.798 --> 00:00:24.446
Tool misuse may cause the agent to call APIs or perform actions that were not intended.

5
00:00:24.446 --> 00:00:28.756
Excessive permissions may allow small mistakes to become major incidents.

6
00:00:28.756 --> 00:00:36.080
Memory poisoning may corrupt stored context, preferences, notes, or task history that the agent later relies on.

7
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:42.705
Data leakage may occur if the agent retrieves, summarizes, or shares information in the wrong context.

8
00:00:42.705 --> 00:00:53.141
Multi-agent systems can introduce additional risks when one agent influences another, delegates work poorly, or passes along untrusted content as if it were trusted.

9
00:00:53.141 --> 00:00:56.225
These threats should be analyzed through the full system.

10
00:00:56.225 --> 00:00:59.946
The useful question is not only whether the model can be influenced.

11
00:00:59.946 --> 00:01:06.921
It is what data, tools, approvals, memory, and downstream workflows can be reached if influence occurs.
